{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:058b352dff466cfd","name":"Rebel Assault Frigate Mark I","source":{"id":"source:reference-058b352dff466cfd","title":"Rebel Assault Frigate Mark I","revision":18778,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:43:10Z","sha256":"e3df4e6388b01e7cab324f5a6263043164814264122b55ed5322202e31fe7c4e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18778","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Rebel%20Assault%20Frigate%20Mark%20I&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-058b352dff466cfd","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The New Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Republic","referenceId":"reference:e6046dbb57e5abb0"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Rebel Assault Frigate is a unique addition to the Alliance Fleet due to its origins. Though they are hardly recognizable as such, these Alliance craft are heavily modified Imperial ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaughts"]},". Although it is common for the Alliance to modify and adapt ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," to its own specifications, the Rebel Assault Frigate is set apart by the sheer amount of modification that it has seen.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When the Alliance acquired a number of ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruisers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dreadnaught-Class_Heavy_Cruisers"},", the initial excitement was replaced by apprehension. The crew requirements of the old warships were astronomical, especially considering the Alliance's limited pool of available crew. True, the ranks of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"}," swelled with every new atrocity committed by the Empire, but this growth was neither fast nor specialized enough to generate several of the 16,000-member crews that ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaughts"]}," ordinarily require. Something needed to be done in order to make use of the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaughts"]},", which were badly needed if the Alliance was to have a chance of defeating the Empire.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["To begin with, huge amounts of the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught's"]}," superstructure have been removed. Not only does this increase the engine capacity of the vessels, but the reduced mass of the ship greatly increases fuel efficiency. In order to improve the ship's maneuverability, two large solar fins were installed along the frigate's dorsal edge. Even with these adjustments, the crew complement of the frigate would still be too extreme. In order to reduce the number of crewmembers required to operate the frigate, automated systems, including large numbers of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", have been implemented throughout the design. These automated systems reduce the crew requirements of the vessel by nearly sixty percent.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"}," has precious few of these ships in operation, mostly due to the expense of retrofitting captured or salvaged ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruisers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dreadnaught-Class_Heavy_Cruisers"},". Those that have been put into service have performed exceptionally well, with no losses reported prior to the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Endor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Endor"},". Though the extensive automation of the ship systems requires additional maintenance, the trade-off is well worth the extra work.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Compared to the ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dreadnaught-Class_Heavy_Cruiser","referenceId":"reference:0d13a1c3c7f04e82"},", the Rebel Assault Frigate Mark I is slightly less resilient, but this is the only area in which the ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Dreadnaught"]},"-Class Heavy Cruiser"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dreadnaught-Class_Heavy_Cruiser","referenceId":"reference:0d13a1c3c7f04e82"}," exceeds the Mark I's capabilities. Due to its widespread modifications, the Rebel Assault Frigate Mark I has augmented deflector shield capacity, a wider range of weaponry, increased speed, and greater maneuverability.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Because much of the frigate's superstructure has been stripped, it lacks docking bays and landing platforms. To make up for this deficiency, Alliance techs have installed twenty umbilical docking fixtures along the ship's surface, six of which are large enough to accommodate a standard Alliance ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},". The remaining fourteen of these fixtures are better suited to docking ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},". Ships connected to these umbilical fixtures cannot be carried through hyperspace, and can be seriously damaged if an attempt is made to do so.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The only concession make by Rebel techs in regard to smaller ships is the inclusion of a modified ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Gamma"]},"-Class Assault Shuttle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gamma-Class_Assault_Shuttle","referenceId":"reference:960972b9df59d8f0"}," at the top of the frigate's superstructure. When properly docked, the ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Gamma"]},"-Class Assault Shuttle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gamma-Class_Assault_Shuttle","referenceId":"reference:960972b9df59d8f0"}," can accompany the Rebel Assault Frigate Mark I into hyperspace with no adverse effect.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Rebel Assault Frigate Mark I Statistics (CL 16)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Cruiser) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -2; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 13), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 52; +13 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 1,500; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 20; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/S